---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';import {github,contact,href} from '../lib/paths';
---
<Base title="An engineering learning community" description="Join official RBE WaveLab Discussions for questions and learning, report technical bugs through Issues and contact Ahmed Rabie for general collaboration." path="community/"><div class="container"><header class="page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Community</span><h1>Ask clearly.<br/>Share thoughtfully.</h1><p class="lede">A space for students, educators and engineers to discuss transmission lines and the learning process around them.</p></header><div class="grid grid-3 section"><article class="article-card"><span class="eyebrow">Questions & learning</span><h2>Discussions</h2><p>Ask usage questions, explore ideas and share nonconfidential experiments. General, Questions & Help, Ideas & Feature Requests, Experiments & Learning and Announcements keep conversations focused.</p><a class="text-button" href={github+'/discussions'}>Open GitHub Discussions ↗</a></article><article class="article-card"><span class="eyebrow">Technical problems</span><h2>Issues</h2><p>Use Bug Report, Feature Request or Documentation Problem. Include the real version, Windows details, reproduction steps, expected behavior and what actually happened.</p><a class="text-button" href={github+'/issues/new/choose'}>Choose an issue template ↗</a></article><article class="article-card"><span class="eyebrow">General contact</span><h2>Meet the owner</h2><p>For general contact and collaboration, connect with Ahmed Rabie on the approved LinkedIn profile. RBE is a display brand; no separate support organization is implied.</p><a class="text-button" href={contact}>Ahmed Rabie on LinkedIn ↗</a></article></div><div class="split section"><div><h2>A useful place to start.</h2><p>The official Welcome discussion explains the community and the preparation of the first application release. There is no application download or Stable launch announcement yet.</p><a href={github+'/discussions/1'}>Read the community welcome →</a></div><div class="callout warning"><h3>Share ideas, not confidential data.</h3><p>Never post passwords, confidential projects or proprietary engineering data. <a href={href('security/')}>Report security concerns privately</a>. Community support is best-effort with no response-time guarantee.</p></div></div></div></Base>
